WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.190
U-lu-lu-no-lu...

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.700
Spring Off-Campus Study
Guidebook

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.700
<i>Yamabuki High School
April 28th</i>

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:33.010
Tell me, tell me, what color is in season now?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.300
Smiling white

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.720
Tearful blue

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.350
Let's mix them together and find out

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.680
Today is sunny, so take out your canvas

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.440
Have some ice cream and lemon soda

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.110
Then draw some exciting and colorful toppings

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.150
Hey, rough sketch, please

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.030
Let's do a self portrait contest

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.790
Yuno

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:06.290
All right! Don't get grouchy later

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.040
Miyako

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.540
Hiro

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:13.380
When the switch is flipped, I go wa-ha-ha

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.790
Sae

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:19.720
I hope everyone is having a great time

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.260
The race is on

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.060
I've gotta finish my apple quickly

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.640
No, that's not for eating

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.310
Let's take it easy

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:35.280
Fruits are our display models

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.120
So start drawing

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.990
It's our homework

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.540
April 28th: A Round Cabbage

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.880
Miya, hurry up, or the bus is gonna leave.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.010
What is she doing?

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.220
She overslept?

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.800
You tend to take things too easy
when the school is so close by.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.140
Yuno, you should be careful too.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.600
I will.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.480
Here she comes.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.600
Sorry.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.230
You're late, Miya.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.400
Miyako!

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.650
Safe.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.400
Yamabuki High School 1-A

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:23.830
Okay, class. Quiet, please.
I'll be your guide today.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.740
Art Department 1-A

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.120
We'll visit the zoo to learn
about speed sketching.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.040
Okay.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.260
To your left is Berry Mart, a convenience store
that's popular among the Yamabuki students.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:41.760
Coming up on your right is Okada Meat Market.
It's croquette is quite good.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.350
Up next at your left is Minowa Milk Shop
that's known for its calcium-enhanced milk.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.310
Further down on your right is
Oyama Newspaper Delivery,

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:54.730
which has been in business for thirteen years.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.450
Oh, please...

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.450
I'd better be prepared.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.870
Do you get motion sickness, Yunocchi?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.660
No, please!

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.000
Don't say anything like you have a weak
tolerance, or don't like riding in cars.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.090
The worst is to be overly conscious
about motion.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.470
I see. I don't get sick, so... Wow!

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.630
Yunocchi, you look so dashing!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.760
This weakens the impact of what I see.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:30.100
I've taken some pills,
taped a 1-yen coin on my wrist,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.270
put some pickled plum
paste on my belly button,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.900
and also wrote out and swallowed
the character ''human'' on my palm.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.730
Ummm, the last one sounds like it's
for something different.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.200
It feels like a field trip when
we ride in the bus like this.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.830
You're right.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.500
Come to think of it, I was always
assigned to the first row

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.670
whenever we went for a school trip
when I was in elementary school.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.300
The kids who tend to get motion sickness
are usually told to sit up front.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.970
I always got excited the night before
the trip, so I never sleep well.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.140
Really? I conked out right away.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.190
You never even got excited, Miya?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.270
I did, but I had to sleep,
or it'd be rough the next day.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.030
You're right.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.200
Nakayama Zoo

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.740
It's been a long time since I went to the zoo.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.990
Probably since sometime at the beginning
of elementary school.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.160
I think my last visit was during the
later half of elementary school.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.460
Oh Hiro, Sae.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.500
Oh, so you've been waiting for us.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.750
We thought we could go look around together.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.300
Elephants

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.300
Japanese Monkeys

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.300
Aquarium

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.300
Lions

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.300
It's been so long since I went to the zoo.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.760
It's been so long since I went to the zoo.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.670
You too, Sae?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:44.760
What was that?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.050
Didn't you come here for dates?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.600
It's a popular place, isn't it?

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.890
Well, yeah, of course, for dates, yes.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.810
Ummm, well...

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.610
I held my boyfriend's hand, while watching
ice cream and eating a herd of wildebeests.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.570
Good times!

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.700
Sae is totally disturbed.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.830
I wonder if a herd of wildebeests tastes good?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.950
She's so cute.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.040
I wish I could see a herd of
wildebeests for once.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.540
You have to go to a savanna region.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.380
Wow, the elephants are huge.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:27.680
Doesn't the elephants' coarse skin
remind you of something?

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.430
Like what?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
The magnified image of dry skin that you
see on moisturizer commercials.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.310
Now that you mention it...

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.110
When I see elephants,
I get this urge to put on lotion.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.690
I think it would be kinda freaky to see an
elephant with smooth skin.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.570
Hiro would put lotion even on the rhinoceros.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.780
A smooth-skinned rhino...

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.870
Sorry for putting you through such hard times.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.250
Mom, you promised you wouldn't talk about it.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.960
I'll work even harder so you don't
get any more gray hair.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.840
They totally look like it.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.430
Thank you for everything, John.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.800
Japanese Monkey (Cercopithecidae)
Habitat: Japan (Honshu, Shikoku, Kyushu)
Northern End: Shimokita Peninsula
(Northernmost habitat for the monkeys)

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.140
Is he a foreigner?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:18.640
And so John comes to know the shocking
fact that Sachiko is not his real mother.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.100
Oh, that's how your story is
supposed to develop?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:24.150
They're tapirs; so cute.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.610
They look totally opposite
to rice balls, don't they?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:30.660
Opposite to rice balls?
Oh, I see what you mean.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.490
Why are they so precisely black and white?

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:39.580
It must be because it has to blend in with
the environment to stay discreet.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.210
That means...

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.670
That's so wrong.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:50.380
Come to think, they say tapirs
eat up nightmares for you.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.100
Do they pig out?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.600
Well, ummm...

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.270
I said, pigging out...

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:01.190
I like the lions because they're so cute.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.400
Cute? Are they?

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:09.070
Yes, I saw one playing with a toy on TV.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.780
Since then, they look cute.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.030
Well, they are a part of the
feline family after all.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:18.290
So, they'll curl up under the
kotatsu table in winter.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:23.130
A lion under the kotatsu? No one
would be able to get any closer.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.460
Yeah, you'd have to risk your life, wouldn't you?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.880
So, the zoo has marine animals too.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.090
You can see them swim.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.430
Oh! It's a sea lion.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.390
It's a seal, Miya.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.400
Oh my...

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.450
Hey, he loves you.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.030
Loves me?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:56.410
You have to respond properly.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:01.080
Whatever your intentions are, we just met.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.670
Does it mean Sae looks like a seal?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.750
Like which part?

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.340
Umm, glasses?

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.090
We saw all kinds of animals.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.890
Let's have lunch.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:19.470
Since we were going to the zoo,
I shaped apples into rabbits.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.890
I made an elephant with hot dogs.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.770
That looks awesome, Hiro. How did you do it?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.940
I'll show you next time.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:32.320
I cooked mine, instead of buying something.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.870
You made your own lunch?
Oh, that's why you were late.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.450
Ta-da!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.120
What the?!

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.000
I have some mayo, so don't worry.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.880
That's not the point.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.840
A sea otter...

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.420
Enough of your improv jokes.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:56.550
I felt like I became an herbivore after
I finished a whole cabbage.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.850
In that case, I guess it was a suitable
lunch to take to the zoo.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.600
I'd better review today's work.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.270
Your drawings? What?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.110
Can hippos stand like that?

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:09.980
No.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.940
We haven't seen any hippos anyway.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:16.360
That's too much.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:23.120
If it's unrealistic, there's no point in
sketching live animals. Right, Yuno?

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.460
Eh? Umm...

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.420
So, I re-drew it.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.340
But that's...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:43.560
In order to draw realistically, you have to
capture each animal's characteristic features.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.140
Okay.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.350
I think the fastest way to improve
is to study their structure

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:52.110
like bones and muscles that
you tend to overlook.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:58.820
Even so, it's still hard, so you have to
practice by drawing several sketches.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.540
I see. Well, why aren't you drawing anything?

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:10.000
Actually, I'm not good at sketching animals.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:16.210
Ever since my art teacher at junior high
told me my drawings of animals sucked,

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.130
I became rather unconfident
about drawing them.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:19.550
Sae...

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:24.390
Well, the teacher was right,
because I really suck.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:31.610
Maybe so when you were in junior high,
but we just saw the real deal, so maybe...

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.190
The thing is...

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:39.320
I mix realism and my imagination,
so they end up looking cartoon-like.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.530
Art Department 1-A

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.580
How did all of you do? Did you have fun?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.790
Yosshi?!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.370
Don't look.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.710
Oh, that looks great.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:58.050
It captures the wildness of the animal.
I think it's wonderful.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:01.760
Sae?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.020
I remember Sae called Ms. Yoshinoya ''Yosshi.''

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.980
I wonder if that's how she was called last year?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.570
How should we call her this year? Yoshyan?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.950
Why the western dialect?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.990
That was fun.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.080
I want to come here for just for fun,
instead of studying.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:34.790
Huh? Ms.Yoshinoya, we're leaving.
Aren't you getting on?

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:41.800
Well actually, my head is still spinning
because of motion sickness.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.430
Oh, that's why...

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.140
Today was really fun.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.270
I wonder what happened to Ms. Yoshinoya?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.730
She didn't appear during last period.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.690
I hope she got back from the zoo
without incident.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.950
Sensei, sensei!

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.950
Are you all right, Ms. Yoshinoya?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.160
Where am I?

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.910
The Hidamari Apartments.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:17.750
Yuno... guys... What happened?

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.630
Well, actually...

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:24.050
You were holding on to the
apartment sign, looking so sick.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.810
You were tottering and looked unstable,
so we brought you to Hiro's place.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:35.150
I see. I took a taxi, but got struck
by motion sickness anyway.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.690
Oh no, I have to get back to school now.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.400
Oh no, watch out!

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:46.240
You should rest a little longer.
I'll make some tea.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.200
Thank you.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.620
Here you go, miss.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.460
Thank you, Hiro.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.250
I don't know if these suit your taste, but...

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.880
Why are you saying that? It's Hiro's.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.670
It brings back memories.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.130
Hidamari Apartments...

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.890
You've been to Hidamari?

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:13.480
Yes, some of my past students lived here,
just like you guys.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.440
I haven't been here ever since,
so it makes me feel nostalgic.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:21.440
Hiro, you seem to be keeping your place clean.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.860
Totally different from Sae's place.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:27.530
I clean the whole place after I finish writing.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:31.200
Drawing pictures on the wall, carving a relief,

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.120
or setting up weird gear so a basin
will fall from the ceiling...

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.420
You don't seem to be doing
any of those, I suppose.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.960
There's no way we'd do that.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:45.550
Looks like you don't know, but it's famous.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:49.640
The Hidamari Apartments always attracts
weirdos from the Art Department.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.850
Miss, I have a question.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.140
Go ahead, Miyako.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.100
Where do you get your costumes?

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.440
I make them myself.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:05.360
I have to do it in order to
make them fit perfectly.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:10.280
I made this uniform after the idea
popped up in my head last night.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.240
Didn't you have anything else to do
before the off-campus study?

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.660
Wow, so you like cosplay.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.920
Cosplay... What are you talking about?

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.380
Your looks...

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:27.220
This is my formal attire, and not cosplay.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:31.510
She isn't aware that she's cosplaying.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.220
Is that so?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:36.180
Oh, could that be...

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.560
Eternal Seventeen
Ms. Yoshinoya Photo Collection

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.560
Ms. Yoshinoya's photo collection?

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.600
Where did it come from?

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.650
My class made this during
last year's school festival.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:51.320
It was meant to be a joke, but you
still kept it, didn't you, Hiro?

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:57.450
The thing is, 300 copies sold out in 15 minutes!

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.170
It's like a popular band's concert tickets.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.540
Ms. Yoshinoya is that popular?

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.710
Not sure...

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:10.090
It sounds fishy.
She's not a celebrity or anything.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.260
How can a photo collection of a
teacher be sold that fast?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.390
Now that you mention it...

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.850
All kinds of rumors went around.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:22.690
Jonathan Matsuya's Hidamari Diary

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:22.400
Like she's actually an online idol who
goes by Jonathan Matsuya.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:28.150
All the customers were actually
planted by Ms. Yoshinoya.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.690
That's impossible.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:34.570
Something wrong with Matsuya or plants?

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.330
No-Nothing.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:43.000
Not just me; the principal published
his photo book too.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.710
The principal did?!

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.340
That was meant for fun at the festival.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:53.380
It was a unique photo book where you try
to find the principal in the crowd.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.350
Where's the Principal

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.350
Yamabuki High School Principal
Photo Collection

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:02.440
Where...

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:13.400
Wow, amazing. You look so cute.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.530
You're beautiful.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.450
You look young.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.540
How old are you?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.580
Seventeen forever.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:28.420
Thanks for all your help.
I'm going back to school.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.710
Yuno, Miyako, see you tomorrow.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:35.010
Make sure you finish today's drawings.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.890
I wonder if she's all right?

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.390
She was still tottering a bit.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.640
There aren't very many people who aren't
good with riding in cars like her.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:50.530
How was she last year? She was your
homeroom teacher, wasn't she?

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:57.160
When we were in the tenth grade, we went
to a museum to sketch sculptures.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:01.040
I remember she had to give up
near Berry Mart.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.290
That soon?

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.750
So, she endured a bit longer this year.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:12.010
Ms. Yoshinoya is kind of strange
and unique, isn't she?

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:17.090
Speaking of which, when I met her the
first time after the entrance ceremony...

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:22.810
We were told to sit down wherever we wanted,

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.890
but that ended up being our seat arrangement
for the rest of the year.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.770
Ours was like that too.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:31.650
I knew it.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:36.450
The shortest girl in the class ended up
having to sit behind the tallest guy.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.370
So, she had a hard time the entire year.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.660
She's a nice teacher though.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.790
She's very enthusiastic in many different ways.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:49.500
Sometimes she goes overboard and gets
chewed out by the principal.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:55.420
How long has Ms. Yoshinoya been
teaching at Yamabuki High?

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.430
Dunno. Do you?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:03.560
I remember her saying she came to the
school right after she finished college.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.980
We don't know how old she is.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:10.020
She said earlier that she'll be
seventeen forever,

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.940
but she wasn't joking; she's dead serious.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:14.650
Young at heart, right?

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:19.070
But don't you think it's important
as an art teacher?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.580
You have to have the sensitivity
of young people.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:29.500
What do you think about her as an adult?
She's eccentric in many ways.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.040
True.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:36.010
An ordinary teacher wouldn't dress up like a tour
guide when going to an off-campus study.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:41.890
It's kind of difficult to know whether to take it as
a lack of common sense or her uniqueness,

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.890
but I like it.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:50.730
Oh, Ms. Yoshinoya used to always visit
the students who took a sick day.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.860
What? Why?

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.360
Unlike other departments,

00:18:55.360 --> 00:19:00.070
many students in the art department live
away from home just like us, right?

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:07.700
So, she paid a visit and took
care of sick students.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.580
She's so kind.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:14.630
But she doesn't do it any more, right? Why?

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:21.800
Students take a day off for cold and flu, right?

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:29.480
She had to take a day off herself
because she caught a cold.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:34.230
The principal scolded her for
making herself sick.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.110
So, she reluctantly stopped doing that.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.360
I can totally see that happening.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:42.570
She doesn't seem to have a strong
body or a lot of stamina.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:46.240
She doesn't look it, but rumor has it
that she is unexpectedly tough.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:53.290
Apparently, she won a school
marathon a few years ago.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:55.630
Really?

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:57.460
That's a surprise.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.260
It's only a rumor.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:05.090
She has an elusive personality, so there are
many rumors and stories about her.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.680
Most of them are made up by students.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:12.310
Girls like rumors after all.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:18.190
So, the rumor about her being
a street gang member is untrue?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.530
That's just one of many rumors.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:26.490
I heard that she was once the power-eating
champion of western Japan

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.160
for finishing 90 plates of sushi in 30 minutes.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.960
They say she's an heiress to a large corporation,

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.130
or a world-famous designer
under a different name.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.500
She's even seeking a debut in Hollywood.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:46.180
She smashed a rock with one punch,
tamed a wild horse,

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:49.350
or saved an old lady from getting hit
by a truck in the nick of time.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.610
Watch out!

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:07.110
Impossible, definitely not her.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:09.660
They're all rumors after all.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:16.290
Whatever she wears, she looks like
she's wearing a costume for fun.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:21.590
Sorry, I forgot something.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.340
Oh, one thing...

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:27.720
I didn't save an old lady.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.510
It was a little boy.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.890
She was joking, right?

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.980
That was fun.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:44.190
Come to think of it, not just the zoo,

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:47.910
but I haven't been to the aquarium
for a while either.

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:50.240
I want to go with everyone some time.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.740
Ms. Yoshinoya...

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.160
After hearing all kinds of stories
from Sae and Hiro,

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:59.040
I'm even more confused as to
who she really is.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:04.460
But I feel like I'll be able to have fun
in the classroom for a year.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.760
End of April 28th

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.760
To Be Continued

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:21.440
It eventually fades into the tall sky

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:23.070
The voices

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:27.860
Bubble up and fade away

00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:31.280
Fade away

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:35.950
They return to where they belong

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:44.460
And fuse together as they sparkle and collide

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:49.970
This body feels like one entity

00:22:49.970 --> 00:22:53.140
Yet, it's made of infinity

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.520
Caught a falling drop of water

00:22:56.520 --> 00:23:02.520
And now I'm taking a closer look

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:05.190
Awakening Drive

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:09.610
Dash into the sky in our bare feet

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.820
Close your eyes, can you see it?

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:16.990
It's a rainbow bridge, let's run toward it

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:18.700
Awakening Drive

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:23.000
A dazzling spark will break a star into pieces

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:31.220
Scattering across the sky and falling,
now in my hands

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:37.810
I have a piece of a dream, shining so bright

00:23:37.900 --> 00:24:06.810
Next Episode

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:43.070
I have something I want to confess now.

00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:44.570
You do too, Yuno?

00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:45.620
I have one, too.

00:23:45.620 --> 00:23:47.950
What? What's the matter so suddenly?

00:23:47.990 --> 00:23:50.290
Here goes! Three, two, one...

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:51.000
Thank you everyone!

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:51.750
I'll do my best with the diet!
Thank you everyone!

00:23:51.750 --> 00:23:53.330
I'll do my best with the diet!
Hidamari Apartments, banzai!

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:55.630
Well, I... umm....

00:23:56.460 --> 00:24:00.800
Next time is
''December 25th: Goodbye, Ume-Sensei''

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:01.930
What?!

00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:06.810
We'll be waiting at the Hidamari Apartments,
so please, join us again.
